    </div>
    <p>Try the layered read on these two boards: every arrow touching an outside edge with a clear run is layer one; every arrow behind it is layer two. Dense boards like the second one are exactly where the single-blocker rule (Step 4) earns its keep.</p>


    <h2>How This Walkthrough Compares</h2>
    <p>Arrows – Puzzle Escape walkthroughs come in three flavors. Here is the honest breakdown of what each one is good for.</p>
